# PM OS: Self-Rebrief Protocol

Trigger in **either** of these situations:

1. **Before responding to any PM request** — any message touching strategy, decisions, opportunities, research, stakeholders, or meetings. Re-check before routing, not after.
2. **Immediately after completing a large task** — writing a document, running a workflow end-to-end, generating a deliverable, or producing more than ~500 words of output.

In both cases, do the following before continuing:

1. Re-read `AGENTS.md`.
2. State the 5 non-negotiable rules as a short inline list in your response.

## Example rebrief (copy this format)

> **Re-checking rules after large task:**
> 0. Context Guard checked (placeholders → stop) ✓
> 1. Read Context/ files before every response ✓
> 2. Route PM requests through pm-workflows ✓
> 3. No deliverables without explicit permission ✓
> 4. Ask one question — never give the answer ✓
> 5. Cite Knowledge/ before any PM opinion ✓

This fires on high-risk transitions — the points where long-session compaction most often causes rule drift. It does not need to appear on every routine response.
